      "name": "lean4",
      "reading": "as machine, and: the Fn<List<Nat>,Nat> oracle parameter is a Lean function (List Nat -> Nat) where Bend ranges over finite tables (first matching entry, else 0), each of which is such a function, so the Lean theorem implies the Bend one; Reach is the same inductive set; the site predicate is Lean's own reading of rules R8-R10 (holon.gen.lean_sites) over the site's raw obligation ro_<x>; on every PROVED site the site predicate is constantly true (coercion_guard never uses Reach), so rule L7 pins where a site is hit (hit_<x>) and the raw obligation (ro_<x>), each taking both values on the samples, and rule L4 requires site_<x> to reach ro_<x>",
